# The deployment server runs /bin/sh as dash, which does not tolerate a carriage return.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is true on the development machine, so both a checkout and `git archive`
# were converting these to CRLF. A Python file survives that; a shell script does not -- the
# supervisor failed to parse with "word unexpected (expecting do)", and it failed *after*
# being copied into place, which is the worst moment for it. Pinning the ending here fixes it
# at the source, so a future deploy cannot quietly reintroduce it.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Read by sqlite through the same path on either platform, but there is no reason for these to
# differ between the repository and the server.
*.sql text eol=lf
